                       "type":  "heading",
                       "data":  {
                                    "level":  2,
                                    "text":  "SQL Server Data Types — Overview"
                                }
                   },
                   {
                       "type":  "paragraph",
                       "data":  {
                                    "text":  "In SQL Server, a column, variable, and parameter holds a value associated with a type, known as a data type. A data type is an attribute that specifies the type of data that these objects can store — such as integers, character strings, monetary values, date and time, and more."
                                }
                   },
